yield: per-serve
notes: |
  The classic 3:2:1 — prosecco : aperol : soda. Masses below are that ratio at a normal
  wine-glass serve.

  Pairs with breakfast/sourdough-skillet — the bright bitter orange cuts through the creamy
  feta.

  Prosecco first, aperol second. Pour the aperol in after and it sits under the bubbles and
  mixes itself; do it the other way round and you have to stir, which kills the fizz.
ingredients:
  - item: prosecco
    mass: 90
    qty: 3
    unit: part
  - item: aperol
    mass: 60
    qty: 2
    unit: part
  - item: soda water
    mass: 30
    qty: 1
    unit: part
  - item: orange slice
    note: to garnish
steps:
  - big wine glass, filled with ice
  - prosecco first, then aperol, then a splash of soda
  - orange slice in
